ENTITY TOKEN :
0 - empty
1 - WALL
2 - BARRACKS
3 - SUPPLY_DEPOT
4 - COMMAND_CENTER
5 - WORKER_UNIT
6 - ENEMY_WORKER_UNIT
8 - ENEMY_COMBAT_UNIT
9 - COMBAT_UNIT

After that we will need to refactor the TileMap to include separator for arbitrary # of Entities


AbstractUnit :
implement IControllableUnit
WORKER_UNIT
    => Commands :
       moveTo, Attack, Gather, Repair     (Go to PlacementHelper, waitForInput, WaitMenu)

                Attack
                    if intArr is blocked, take a random close point and updateSensing anyway
                    else no Blocked go to point and updateSensing anyway 

                stop         (just stop movement, snap to grid)
       (Gather, Repair print NotImplemented yet)
       buildMenu
           barracksConstruct, SupplyDepotConstruct    (Go to PlacementHelper inside BuildingManager, waitForInput, WaitMenu)

COMBAT_UNIT
    => Commands :
       moveTo, Attack, Gather, Repair     (Go to PlacementHelper, waitForInput, WaitMenu)
       stop         (just stop movement, snap to grid)



When we press a command from CommandActionListener we setMode of navigation inside MouseEventHandler
From this navigation mode we, if constraint are respected, we issueCommand the correct way

Ex: CommandActionListener -> MouseEventHandler -> WorkerUnit
